    <!-- Detailed Contextual Help Dialogs (?) -->
    <string name="help_strategy_library_title">Strategy Guide</string>
    <string name="help_strategy_library_body">[Overview]\nConfigure daily matching goals, per-element rules, column ameliorations, and leader traits here. All changes auto-save and stack with active wave shields; tap Reset anytime to restore defaults.</string>
    <string name="help_basic_steps_title">Step Budget &amp; Solver Compute</string>
    <string name="help_basic_steps_body">[Priority: Wave Shields &gt; Strategy Override &gt; System]\nSettings defines system defaults. Keep Follow System or adjust values here to override; active step shields always take highest priority.\n\n[Step Limit]\nMaximum moves per path (8–300). 30–60 steps suit 6×5 boards; 80–150 suit 6×8 or complex puzzles/crosses.\n\n[Solver Compute]\nControls how many candidate routes are explored per step (40–600). Higher values find stronger combos and hard-shield paths at slightly longer solve time.</string>
    <string name="help_engine_settings_title">Solver Engine &amp; Priority Hierarchy</string>
    <string name="help_engine_settings_body">[Priority: Wave Shields &gt; Strategy Override &gt; System]\nGlobal Steps and Solver Compute here act as system defaults. Strategy overrides take precedence, and active wave shields take highest priority.\n\n• Global Max Steps: default move limit per swipe path (8–300).\n• Solver Compute: number of candidate routes explored per step; higher values find stronger paths at slightly longer solve time.\n• Hold-Reveal Animation Timeout: max wait (ms) for hidden \'?\' orbs to flip open (exits early once revealed; not solve time).\n• Post-Reveal Solve Time Budget: search time budget after the board reveals (0.15–3.5s, default 0.4s); larger budgets explore deeper routes for long-timer teams or hard shields.\n• Pre-Swipe Countdown: optional countdown seconds before swiping.</string>
    <string name="help_goal_policy_title">Matching Goals &amp; Search Policy</string>
    <string name="help_goal_policy_body">[Global Goal]\nGuides overall scoring toward Max Combo, 3/4/5 distinct colors, or 5/6/7/8/9-orb groups.\n\n[Multi-Orb Handling]\n• Max Combo: splits surplus same-color orbs into more combos.\n• Max Orbs: clears as many orbs of that color as possible.\n• Single Group: matches just one group to conserve orbs or steps.\n\n[Insufficient Orbs &amp; Search Style]\n• Match Anyway / Reserve Orbs: decides whether to make a normal 3-match or save orbs when too few exist for a target shape.\n• Best Result: finds the highest-scoring solution within budget.\n• First Match: returns as soon as all hard shields are satisfied.</string>
    <string name="help_elem_matrix_title">Per-Element Rules Matrix</string>
    <string name="help_elem_matrix_body">Configure 4 rules independently for Water, Fire, Wood, Light, Dark, and Heart (tap Reset All to restore every row to defaults):\n\n1. Shape (tap to pick): Auto, Split 3, 2+, 4+..9+, Row, Col, Cross, L, T, 2×2, or Clear All.\n2. Priority: Normal, High (prioritize matching), or Keep (save orbs).\n3. Timing: Any, 1st (must match Wave 1), Stack (forbid Wave 1, allow cascade), or Ban (forbid all).\n4. Min: minimum run length from 1-Match to 5-Match for special leaders.\n\n[Leader Attribute Link]\nEnable Heart+All, Light+Dark, or W+F+G when your leader links attributes so combo counts match in-game rules.</string>
    <string name="help_columns_title">Column Amelioration Guide</string>
    <string name="help_columns_body">[Purpose]\nSets vertical match length targets (Off / 3 / 4 / 5 orbs) for columns 1–6.\n\n[Scenarios]\nTriggers vertical Sword/Heart ameliorations or satisfies column-match enemy shields.</string>
    <string name="help_start_char_title">Start Position &amp; Character Orb</string>
    <string name="help_start_char_body">[Start Position]\nDefault Any Start, or lock to Bottom-Left / Bottom-Right for fixed-origin stages.\n\n[Character Orb Pull]\nSelect Slot 1–6 to pull that member\'s Character Orb vertically into the board (initial pull does not cost a move), ideal for Character-Orb terrain stages.</string>
    <string name="help_strategy_switches_title">Advanced Strategy Switches</string>
    <string name="help_strategy_switches_body">• Force Split 3-Orb Groups: splits groups into 3-orb combos for higher count.\n• First-Wave Combos Only: scores Wave 1 only without relying on cascades.\n• Allow 8-Direction Diagonal Matches: enables diagonal matching for leaders with that skill.\n• Prioritize Enchanted / Race: prefers clearing Enchanted or Race runestones.\n• Allow Hitting Weathered: disables weathered avoidance when intentionally clearing weathered states.</string>
    <string name="help_active_shields_title">Active Wave Shields</string>
    <string name="help_active_shields_body">Displays all temporary wave shields currently active.\nTap any pill to remove it, or tap Clear Shields to clear all temporary wave rules.</string>
    <string name="help_combo_shield_title">Combo Shield Rules &amp; Modifiers</string>
    <string name="help_combo_shield_body">[Primary Combo Rule (Mutually Exclusive)]\n• Min Total (≥ N): counts Wave 1 plus cascades.\n• Min 1st-Wave (≥ N): counts Wave 1 combos only.\n• 1st Elem Groups (≥ N): counts Wave 1 elemental combos only (excludes Heart).\n• Exact Total (= N): final total combos must equal N while avoiding skyfall risk.\n• Exact 1st-Wave (= N): Wave 1 combos must equal N.\n• 1st Same / 1st Distinct: Wave 1 matches of the same or distinct kinds (Heart wildcard).\n• Zero Combo: makes 0 matches to pass a turn safely.\n• Odd / Even Combo: requires odd or even combos (selectable 1st Wave or Total).\n\n[Structural Modifiers (Stackable)]\n• Equal 1st Combos / Attr: every matched attribute in Wave 1 has the same combo count.\n• No Cascade (W1): disables Wave 2+ cascades.\n• 2nd Wave Cascade: requires at least N cascade combos in Wave 2.\n• Same-Attr Groups: requires at least N Wave-1 groups of one attribute.\n• Multi-Attr Equal: requires 2–6 selected attributes to match equally in Wave 1.</string>
    <string name="help_elem_count_title">Attribute &amp; Orb-Count Rules</string>
    <string name="help_elem_count_body">[Min Distinct &amp; Required Attributes]\n• Min Distinct (≥ 2–6): matches at least N different attributes of any color.\n• Required Attributes: matches every selected color, with per-color Enchanted (+) toggles.\n\n[Attribute Restrictions]\n• Anti-1st Stack: forbids Wave-1 matches while allowing Wave-2 cascades.\n• Forbid All: forbids matching in any wave.\n• Clear All 1st: clears every orb of the selected color in Wave 1.\n• Unmatchable: marks attributes sealed by unmatchable debuffs.\n\n[Orb Count &amp; Special Runestones]\n• Exact Orbs: matches an exact Wave-1 orb total.\n• Full-Board 1st Clear: clears every matchable orb on Wave 1.\n• Enchanted Rune 1st: eliminates at least one Enchanted runestone in Wave 1.\n• Race Rune 1st: eliminates a Race runestone, with optional 7-race filter.\n• Character Rune 1st: includes the Character Runestone in a Wave-1 match.\n• Avoid Weak/Evil/Thorn: forbids eliminating Weakened, Evil Energy, or Blood-Thorn runestones.\n• Luminous Rune 1st: clears Luminous runestones in Wave 1.\n(Electrified, Frozen, Blood-Drain, Bomb, Locked, and Foam hazards are handled automatically once detected or marked.)</string>
    <string name="help_puzzle_shape_title">Puzzle &amp; Shape Shield Rules</string>
    <string name="help_puzzle_shape_body">[Puzzle Shield]\n• Normal Puzzle: fills the golden puzzle frame with same-color matches; external same-color orbs may touch.\n• Strict Puzzle: fills the frame with NO external same-color orbs touching the boundary.\n• Enchanted &amp; Attribute: independently require Enchanted runestones or a specific color inside the puzzle.\n• Shape Source: defaults to Auto-Detect Frame, or pick a preset shape template when effects obscure the frame.\n\n[Standalone Shape Shields]\n• Cross Shield: 1/2/3 crosses; multi-cross supports Distinct Colors and lets you pick 1–3 specific cross colors (e.g. Water + Fire dual cross). Reducing cross count resets excess colors automatically.\n• L-Shape / T-Shape / 2×2 Square / All Cols ≥ 4: builds the target geometric match in Wave 1.</string>
    <string name="help_path_hazard_title">Path, Terrain &amp; Step Shields</string>
    <string name="help_path_hazard_body">• Burning Trail Protection: configures trail length (Full or 6 cells) and max allowed hits.\n• Start-to-End: auto-detects green start and red end vortexes (or mark manually in Board Editor).\n• Step Limit / Step Range: caps maximum steps or enforces an exact [min–max] step window.\n• Trail Corrosion: forbids revisiting any cell already traversed.\n• Minimize Steps: finds the shortest path that satisfies active shields.\n• Char-Orb Terrain: routes through Character-Orb pass tiles and ends on stop tiles.\n• 6×8 Long-Step: extends step and compute budget for 6×8 expanded boards.</string>

